<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">Notes :ttttttttt   n1tThe Consolidated financial results include results of Bata India Ltd. (the Holding Company), Bata Properties Limited, Coastal Commercial &amp; Exim Limited and Way Finders Brands Limited (the subsidiaries).   n2tThe Consolidated financial results of the Group are prepared in accordance with the requirements of Ind AS 110  Consolidated Financial Statements .  n3tThe above consolidated results were reviewed by the Audit Committee and approved by the Board of Directors at the Board Meeting held on 25th May 2020.  n4tIn second quarter, the Company has elected to exercise the option permitted under section 115BAA of the Income Tax Act,1961 as introduced by the Taxation Laws (Amendment) Ordinance, 2019. Accordingly, the Company has recognised Provision for Income Tax for the quarter and year ended 31st March 2020 and re- measured its Deferred Tax Assets basis the rate prescribed in the said section. The impact of this change has been recognised over the period from 1 July 2019 to 31 March 2020.  n5tRevenue from operations for the quarter ended 31st March 2020 of Rs. 6205.74 million have decreased by 9% over the corresponding period last year primarily due to lockdown of the Company's stores in last fortnight of March 2020 as per government directives for COVID 19.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
